<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Replay aligned audio, S1 requests, System-2 reasoning progress and feedback from local duplex run traces."><title>Trajectory viewer · AI2AI Duplex</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../assets/site.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../assets/trajectory/viewer.css"><script defer src="../assets/trajectory/viewer.js"></script></head>
<body>
<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to trajectory</a>
<header class="site-nav"><div class="nav-inner"><a class="brand" href="../index.html">AI2AI Duplex</a>{{NAV}}</div></header>
<main id="main"><div class="container">
<header class="hero viewer-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Experiments · Audio-only trajectory · 7 October 2026</p><h1>User → S1 → S2 → Talker.</h1><p class="lede">Inspect the actual user recording, S1 outputs, buffered S2 text, delivered guidance and Talker waveform. Empty text is shown as (silent); no acknowledgment is invented.</p><p class="meta"><a href="index.html">All experiments</a> · Static viewer · Files are read locally and never uploaded</p></header>
{{EXAMPLE_INTRO}}
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="load-title"><h2 id="load-title">Choose the evidence</h2><div class="load-panel" id="drop-zone"><button class="button primary" id="load-real" type="button">Recorded S2 wait</button><label class="button" for="trace-file">Choose local trajectory.json<input id="trace-file" type="file" accept=".json,application/json"></label><button class="button" id="load-demo" type="button">Synthetic viewer demo</button><a class="button" href="../research/trajectory-example.json" download>Download measured example</a><span>Or drop a JSON trace here.</span></div><p id="load-status" role="status" class="meta">Loading recorded example…</p><div class="callout" id="evidence-note"><strong>Recorded example</strong><p>Two jobs provide separate clocks: measured client events for the S2 wait, and input-chunk progress for the continued S1 reply.</p></div><noscript><p>This interactive viewer requires JavaScript. The recorded result and source notes remain readable.</p></noscript></section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="timeline-title"><h2 id="timeline-title">A · Follow the continuous interaction</h2><h3 id="run-title">Recorded S2 wait</h3><p id="clock-note" class="meta"></p><div class="transport"><button id="play" type="button" class="button primary">Replay timing</button><button id="reset" type="button" class="button">Rewind</button><label>Speed <select id="speed"><option value="0.5">0.5×</option><option value="1" selected>1×</option><option value="2">2×</option><option value="5">5×</option><option value="10">10×</option></select></label><label><input type="checkbox" id="warmup"> Include startup</label><label>Zoom <input type="range" id="zoom" min="1" max="5" value="1" step="1"></label><output id="time-label">0.000 s</output></div><label class="scrub-label" for="scrub">Timeline cursor <input id="scrub" type="range" min="0" max="10" value="0" step="0.001"></label><figure class="trajectory-figure"><div class="timeline-scroll" id="timeline-scroll"><svg id="timeline" role="img" aria-labelledby="svg-title svg-description"><title id="svg-title">Time-aligned layer events</title><desc id="svg-description">Client request spans, received progress events and optional browser audition clips.</desc></svg></div><figcaption>Figure 1. Measured client events in the selected run clock. Rows start with User, S1, S2 and Talker. Request blocks contain the generated text received at their end, or (silent) for an empty tts field. These are request intervals, not word timestamps; dots show received progress. Dashed gray bands annotate a test condition or missing S1 call. Green dashed S2 blocks show the latest delivered guidance retained in S1 context; they are not S2 compute durations. (Silent) refers to empty speech text; it does not certify that a decoder waveform is acoustically silent. Synthetic demo and imported audio traces can also show hatched browser audition spans; these are replay schedules, not measured playback. User audio bars show recording duration at a browser audition anchor, not a live microphone timeline. Scroll horizontally to read the content; use Zoom for detail.</figcaption></figure><div class="stat-grid" id="stats" aria-label="Trace statistics"></div><div class="inspector-grid"><article class="card"><h3>Selected event</h3><p id="selection-title">Click a bar or event marker.</p><pre id="event-detail">No event selected.</pre></article><article class="card"><h3>State at the cursor</h3><p id="active-layers">No active requests.</p><dl class="cursor-state"><dt>S1 user transcription (ASR)</dt><dd id="s1-asr">Not received yet.</dd><dt>S1 generated speech text (tts)</dt><dd id="s1-text">Not received yet.</dd><dt>S2 reasoning progress</dt><dd id="reasoning-progress">No received reasoning deltas.</dd><dt>S2 streamed text · still buffered</dt><dd id="s2-text">Not received yet.</dd><dt>Guidance actually delivered to S1</dt><dd id="s2-delivered">No guidance delivered yet.</dd><dt>Latest control event</dt><dd id="control-text">None.</dd></dl></article></div></section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="continuation-title"><h2 id="continuation-title">B · Earlier text-only continuation diagnostic</h2><p class="section-intro">Job 1816006 replays the saved S2 answer and continues 24 input chunks. This is a separate text-generation test; S2’s answer is already available. Figure 2 uses input-audio progress, not phase A’s wall clock or spoken-word timestamps.</p><div class="case-toolbar"><label for="reply-case">Diagnostic case <select id="reply-case"></select></label><button class="button" id="chunk-play" type="button">Replay text chunks</button><button class="button" id="chunk-reset" type="button">First chunk</button></div><p id="case-note" class="meta"></p><p><strong>Supplied S2 answer:</strong> <span id="reply-command"></span></p><label class="scrub-label" for="chunk-cursor">Input chunk <input id="chunk-cursor" type="range" min="0" max="23" value="23" step="1"><output id="chunk-label"></output></label><figure class="trajectory-figure"><div class="chunk-legend"><span class="empty">Empty tts</span><span class="prefix">Preface</span><span class="answer">S2 answer</span><span class="followup">Follow-up</span></div><div class="chunk-matrix-scroll"><div class="chunk-grid" id="chunk-grid" aria-label="User, S1, S2 and Talker by input chunk"></div></div><figcaption>Figure 2. Aligned content rows for each 480 ms input chunk: User, S1, S2 and Talker. The replay inputs are digital silence; the saved S2 guidance arrives once at chunk zero; Talker was not run in this older text diagnostic. Click a chunk or replay the sequence to inspect the accumulated reply. Green chunks contain the supplied S2 answer; blue shows a preface, amber an extra follow-up whose quality is unvalidated, and gray an empty tts field. No speech waveform was generated in this test.</figcaption></figure><div class="inspector-grid"><article class="card"><h3>S1 text generated in this chunk</h3><p class="reply-fragment" id="chunk-fragment"></p><p class="meta" id="chunk-detail"></p><details><summary>Transcription and control fields</summary><pre id="chunk-fields"></pre></details></article><article class="card"><h3>S1 reply accumulated so far</h3><p class="reply-transcript" id="chunk-transcript" aria-live="polite"></p><p class="meta" id="answer-status"></p></article></div><p class="meta">Historical allocation: 1 × A100 80 GB, GPU 0 S1 Thinker only. No Talker or live S2 service in this replay. Phases A and B ran separately; their maximum allocation was 2 GPUs, not 3.</p></section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="audio-title"><h2 id="audio-title">Audio audition</h2><p class="section-intro">The actual user recording and full continuous Talker waveform are included. Pre-guidance audio is also available: S1’s tts fields were empty there, and a nonzero waveform does not establish spoken acknowledgment. Select a clip and use its native playback controls. The timeline cursor follows its audio position when an anchor is available. This is a browser replay clock; the run does not record speakers, network playout or microphone capture.</p><p class="meta">Input audio is a public research-dataset excerpt, not a private user recording: <a href="https://github.com/keonlee9420/DailyTalk">DailyTalk</a> by Keon Lee, Kyumin Park and Daeyoung Kim; stereo adaptation from <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/kyutai/DailyTalkContiguous">Kyutai DailyTalkContiguous</a>. We extracted the right channel’s first 10 seconds. This adapted clip is supplied under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>; see the <a href="../research/audio-provenance.json">verified source hashes and transformation record</a>.</p><div class="audio-panel"><label for="clip-select">Audio clip <select id="clip-select"></select></label><audio id="clip-player" controls preload="metadata"></audio><p id="clip-note" class="meta"></p><figure class="waveform-figure"><svg id="waveform" role="img" aria-labelledby="wave-title" viewBox="0 0 800 90"><title id="wave-title">Selected clip waveform envelope</title></svg><figcaption>Figure 3. Amplitude envelope of the selected recorded or synthetic audio clip; this figure does not establish acoustic word alignment or actual speaker playback.</figcaption></figure></div><details><summary>Run metadata and archived text</summary><pre id="run-metadata"></pre></details></section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="events-title"><h2 id="events-title">Event ledger</h2><div class="filter"><label for="event-search">Find events</label><input id="event-search" type="search" placeholder="Layer, command, label or text"><output id="event-count"></output></div><div class="table-wrap event-table"><table><caption>Table 1. Exact boundaries in the selected trace clock, stated above Figure 1 and in metadata. Request end means response received; stream progress means delta received. Absence bands are annotations from the request inventory.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Layer</th><th scope="col">Start (s)</th><th scope="col">End (s)</th><th scope="col">Event</th></tr></thead><tbody id="event-rows"></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="capture-title"><h2 id="capture-title">Capture and interpretation</h2><div class="card-grid"><article class="card"><h3>Real runs</h3><p>The DuplexOmni driver now flushes <code>events.jsonl</code> during a run and exports a portable <code>trajectory.json</code> with embedded WAV clips on exit. Copy that JSON to your machine and load it above. A shared monotonic clock covers startup, S1, S2 and Talker.</p><p>S2 progress records received character counts and final answer text. Its internal reasoning text is not stored. S2 streamed text is shown separately from guidance delivery. Only closed, complete clauses are sent to S1. Thinker returns one structured output per request; no spoken-word alignment is inferred.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Two clocks to keep separate</h3><p>Wall time answers when a request started, when a delta arrived and when an audio file became available. Audio content time answers where you are within a recording. The cursor links them using an explicitly labeled audition anchor.</p><p>The current controlled test submits whole audio turns, then returns whole WAV files. A true streaming trajectory also needs chunk input timestamps, codec emission times and actual playback timestamps; those are not inferred here.</p></article></div><details><summary>Portable trace schema and export command</summary><p>The viewer accepts <code>duplex-trajectory/v1</code> JSON containing <code>evidence</code>, <code>lanes</code>, <code>events</code>, <code>media</code>, <code>metadata</code> and <code>limitations</code>. Events use <code>start</code> / <code>end</code> seconds and a <code>lane</code> ID; media use embedded <code>data:audio/wav;base64,…</code>, duration and an optional wall-time anchor. Remote media URLs are not fetched.</p><pre>python scripts/trajectory.py exp/inference/duplexomni/audio_turn_system2_JOB_ID</pre><p>Existing run folders without event logs export as <code>summary_only</code>. Their audio remains listenable, but the viewer shows no fabricated timeline.</p></details><h3>Trace limitations</h3><ul id="limitations"></ul><p class="meta">This page is a local inspection tool. The hosted demo contains no dataset speech, private paths, model checkpoints or live inference endpoint.</p></section>
<footer class="site-footer"><p>AI2AI Duplex · <a href="index.html">All experiments</a> · <a href="../index.html">Literature review</a> · <a href="../research/trajectory-schema.md">Trace schema</a></p></footer>
</div></main><script id="demo-trace" type="application/json">{{DEMO}}</script><script id="recorded-example" type="application/json">{{EXAMPLE}}</script>
</body></html>
